Subject: [PATCH] Copy gather tails as words and map tiny rank rows directly

Upstream base: 6ee0d76e987ab5a13a64032582bc3da945ce3eae. Rationale: remove byte-per-thread copies, device division and rank-one materialization. Aligned opaque words preserve payloads; tiny tails use a warp per rank/row with no division, larger tails use exact host-computed reciprocals. Quality: explicit validated bounds and disjoint outputs, unchanged packed path. Tests: 10,070 integer-reference checks, 147 gather tests per boot on previous variant; final direct-grid two-boot tests and strict timings pending. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
